# What the relayer image does NOT get, and why each exclusion is load-bearing.
#
# `docker build` tars the working directory and sends it to the daemon. Unfiltered that is ~600 MB
# here, same as the Vercel upload that produced `.vercelignore` — this file is its sibling and the
# two must stay in agreement about `reference/`, which is the bulk of it.
#
# THE FIRST ENTRY IS THE SECURITY ONE. `.env` holds a funded signer's private key. The relayer
# reads its key from the process environment (server.ts's header explains why), and on Fly that
# environment comes from `fly secrets set`, never from a file baked into a layer. An image layer is
# not a secret: it is content-addressed, cached, pullable by anyone with registry access, and it
# survives every later `rm`. Excluding it here is what keeps the key out of the image.
.env
.env.*

# Runtime state of THIS machine's relayer — a hashed-visitor salt and two spend ledgers. The
# deployed relayer keeps its own on a Fly volume (`/data`, see fly.toml); shipping the local copy
# would seed production with a developer's counters and, worse, with a salt that has been on a
# laptop.
.relayer/

# 366 MB of upstream clones read by humans and research, never by the build.
reference/

# Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile — a macOS `node_modules` is not a Linux one.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Planning artifacts, research, and the workflow engine. Not build inputs.
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
context/
docs/
# evidence/ WAS here, and its exclusion was the bug: the allowlist and keeper read contract
# addresses from evidence/*.json at boot, so an image without the directory runs with no
# MessageBook, Markets or Launch — "not a build input" was simply false for these files.

# The web app builds and deploys elsewhere (Vercel). The relayer image only needs the two
# packages, the root manifest and `vendor/`.
apps/web/dist/
.vercel/
.git/
.claude/
.agents/

# Never a build input, and `*.log` is already gitignored — it exists so a stray local log cannot
# change the build context hash and bust the layer cache.
*.log
.DS_Store
